WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.493 --> 00:00:03.114
- [Voiceover] We all know
added sugar isn't healthy,

00:00:03.114 --> 00:00:05.592
but is avoiding it worth it?

00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:07.258
We wanted to find out,

00:00:07.258 --> 00:00:09.289
so we asked three sugar addicts

00:00:09.289 --> 00:00:11.139
to change their diets for a month

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:15.040
to see what happens
when you give up sugar.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.036
("Allure Amour")

00:00:20.036 --> 00:00:22.987
- For breakfast I usually
have like a Starburst.

00:00:24.414 --> 00:00:27.054
I'm interested in this challenge because

00:00:27.054 --> 00:00:28.640
as I started working in office jobs

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.271
I went from 125 to 165, so.

00:00:33.271 --> 00:00:34.922
- Should I not be drinking this thing?

00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:38.514
I feel bad for everyone in my life

00:00:38.514 --> 00:00:41.744
because it does feel like
my mood a lot of the time

00:00:41.744 --> 00:00:44.487
is directly tied to my diet.

00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:45.848
- I'll get stressed out.

00:00:45.848 --> 00:00:47.891
I get headaches if I don't eat sugar.

00:00:49.891 --> 00:00:51.761
I'm 27, I think it's time

00:00:51.761 --> 00:00:53.283
to start eating like an adult

00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:54.992
and not like a 16 year old.

00:00:54.992 --> 00:00:59.992
("Allure Amour")

00:01:06.612 --> 00:01:11.590
- It's just been an emotional
roller coaster of a week.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.887
I (bleep) up

00:01:13.887 --> 00:01:15.856
and ordered an old fashion.

00:01:15.856 --> 00:01:18.070
What do I drink to get caffeine?

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.473
Soda.

00:01:19.473 --> 00:01:20.895
- [Voiceover] You could drink coffee.

00:01:20.895 --> 00:01:22.968
- I don't want to drink black coffee.

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.405
Black coffee straight is shitty.

00:01:25.405 --> 00:01:28.798
- Super Bowl sucks 'cause
I just got to sit there

00:01:28.798 --> 00:01:32.292
and eat like corn chips
that tasted really crappy.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.116
And then today, work was free cupcake day.

00:01:35.116 --> 00:01:36.824
This sucks.

00:01:36.824 --> 00:01:38.246
- Went to Disneyland yesterday.

00:01:38.246 --> 00:01:39.748
Everyone was eating tasty treats.

00:01:39.748 --> 00:01:41.497
I couldn't have any of these tasty treats,

00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:42.959
so I had a pickle.

00:01:45.081 --> 00:01:46.626
- I feel like that weirdo

00:01:46.626 --> 00:01:47.345
'cause I'm in the grocery store

00:01:47.345 --> 00:01:48.746
like looking at the back of everything

00:01:48.746 --> 00:01:50.169
to see what's in it.

00:01:50.169 --> 00:01:51.571
And I never wanted to be that guy,

00:01:51.571 --> 00:01:52.790
and now I'm that guy.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.437
- Any positive changes?

00:01:55.391 --> 00:01:56.965
I don't know, not really.

00:01:58.073 --> 00:02:00.998
- Ugh, I hope it's worth it.

00:02:00.998 --> 00:02:05.998
("Allure Amour")

00:02:06.037 --> 00:02:07.540
- So, last week was really bad,

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.202
but this week I'm kind of used to it.

00:02:10.202 --> 00:02:12.051
And actually slipped up,

00:02:12.051 --> 00:02:14.468
and grabbed a can of Coke and drank it.

00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:17.516
Last night I drank soda
to try to stay up late

00:02:17.516 --> 00:02:18.917
'cause I was doing work.

00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:22.087
And I feel like junk this morning.

00:02:22.087 --> 00:02:26.049
- I have thinned down a bit.

00:02:26.049 --> 00:02:27.918
I've lost a few pounds.

00:02:27.918 --> 00:02:29.056
- I feel like I'm more positive.

00:02:29.056 --> 00:02:30.945
I feel like my energy
levels are more level.

00:02:30.945 --> 00:02:32.570
And I don't have these lows.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:34.074
- This is actually not that bad.

00:02:34.074 --> 00:02:35.314
I feel like, I don't know,

00:02:35.314 --> 00:02:36.695
I feel like I could do this.

00:02:36.695 --> 00:02:41.164
I feel like I can actually
stop eating so much sugar.

00:02:41.164 --> 00:02:46.164
("Allure Amour")

00:02:46.293 --> 00:02:48.080
- I lost five pounds.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:48.852
That's crazy.

00:02:48.852 --> 00:02:50.009
Five pounds of fat

00:02:50.009 --> 00:02:52.042
according to the body comp test.

00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:53.647
So yeah, I feel pretty good about

00:02:53.647 --> 00:02:55.679
the direct result.

00:02:55.679 --> 00:02:58.909
- I actually can confidently say

00:02:58.909 --> 00:03:01.580
I don't miss sugar that much.

00:03:02.688 --> 00:03:06.141
Crazy, mind blowing, life changing?

00:03:06.141 --> 00:03:07.847
Yes, all of the above.

00:03:07.847 --> 00:03:09.413
- Planning my meals,

00:03:09.413 --> 00:03:11.384
I'm using all fresh ingredients.

00:03:11.384 --> 00:03:12.339
The cool thing about this diet

00:03:12.339 --> 00:03:15.000
is it's making me cook again,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.000
which I haven't done in an
embarrassingly long time.

00:03:20.018 --> 00:03:21.704
Kind of like looking at what
you're putting in your body,

00:03:21.704 --> 00:03:23.086
looking at the back of the ingredients,

00:03:23.086 --> 00:03:25.423
or just being conscious of it was huge.

00:03:25.423 --> 00:03:26.908
- In the third week I was like

00:03:26.908 --> 00:03:30.441
wow, I'm like happy.

00:03:30.441 --> 00:03:31.682
I'm really happy right now,

00:03:31.682 --> 00:03:34.199
and I feel calm and not stressed out.

00:03:34.199 --> 00:03:35.764
- I drink more water now.

00:03:36.994 --> 00:03:38.710
I am glad I did it.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:39.766
It's all for the better.

00:03:39.766 --> 00:03:41.067
Yeah, I don't want that diabetes.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:42.264
My dad's got it.

00:03:42.264 --> 00:03:43.403
I don't wanna get that.

00:03:43.403 --> 00:03:44.575
Ew.

00:03:44.575 --> 00:03:45.794
- At the beginning I was like

00:03:45.794 --> 00:03:47.772
I can't wait 'til the month is over

00:03:47.772 --> 00:03:49.985
so that I can go back
and eat all the sugar

00:03:49.985 --> 00:03:51.550
that I'm missing.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.887
And now I don't even
think I'm gonna do that.

00:03:53.887 --> 00:03:55.024
I think I'm gonna stick with it

00:03:55.024 --> 00:03:56.264
for a little bit longer.

00:03:56.264 --> 00:03:57.381
(laughs)

00:03:57.381 --> 00:03:58.438
Who am I?

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:02.191
Who am I? (laughs)

00:04:02.191 --> 00:04:06.179
Am I an adult now? (laughs)

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.231
- [Voiceover] It's so good.

00:04:08.231 --> 00:04:13.231
("Allure Amour")

